+ - **Forensic analysis**: Preserving original content while enabling selective sharing of anonymized excerpts (with explicit controls)
+ - **High-security operations**: Environments requiring data minimization and zero-local-retention options
+ - 🔐 **Strong Encryption**: Encrypts full scrape content with AES-256-GCM using a cryptographically secure random nonce for each operation, providing both confidentiality and integrity
+ - 🛡️ **Rigorous PII Removal**: Optionally strips personally identifiable information using comprehensive regex patterns (emails, phone numbers, SSNs, credit cards, IBANs, addresses, names, passport numbers, driver licenses, medical IDs, account numbers, etc.) before encryption - enabling safe sharing when desired
+ - 📋 **Conditional Excerpt Generation**: Generates a short, redacted markdown excerpt (head/tail of text with PII removed) ONLY when explicitly requested via `store_excerpt=true` - enables zero-local-retention mode for highly sensitive operations
+ - 🔓 **Memory-Only Retrieval**: Provides secure decryption and viewing of previously scraped content with **explicit guarantees** that decrypted data exists ONLY in memory during retrieval and is immediately and securely wiped afterward
+ - 📊 **Comprehensive Audit Trail**: Maintains SHA-256 hashes of both encrypted files and excerpts (when generated) for integrity verification and tamper detection
+ - 🧹 **Secure Memory Handling**: Uses industry-standard secure zeroization techniques for decrypted data in memory
+ 1. **Determine Privacy Needs**: Decide whether you need:
+    - **Maximum privacy** (zero local retention): Use `--store-excerpt false`
+    - **Standard privacy** (encrypted storage + shareable excerpt): Use `--store-excerpt true` (default)
+    - **Forensic completeness** (keep all data, disable PII removal): Use `--remove-pii false`
+ 2. **Scrape**: Execute `privacy-scraper scrape --url <url> [--allow-domains domain1,domain2] [--timeout-seconds <seconds>] [--remove-pii true|false] [--store-excerpt true|false]`
+    - Always creates: `vault/<timestamp>.enc` – AES-256-GCM encrypted archive of the full page text
+    - Creates excerpt ONLY when `store_excerpt=true`: `excerpt.md` – a short, redacted summary with PII removed if enabled
+    - Both files include SHA-256 hashes for integrity verification
+ 3. **Share Responsibly**:
+    - If `store_excerpt=true`: Share only the `excerpt.md` file, which contains NO sensitive information when PII removal is enabled
+    - If `store_excerpt=false`: No files to share - maximum privacy maintained
+    - Never share encrypted `.enc` files without explicit authorization and context
+ 4. **Archive**: Preserve the encrypted `.enc` file for long-term storage, compliance records, or future verification (retain SHA-256 hash for integrity verification)
+ 5. **Retrieve Securely**: When needed, decrypt and view content with `privacy-scraper retrieve --id <timestamp> [--verify-wipe]`
+    - **Critical Security Guarantee**: Decrypted text appears ONLY in memory during retrieval
+    - **Memory Wipe Confirmation**: Use `--verify-wipe` to receive explicit confirmation that decrypted data was securely wiped from memory after retrieval
+    - Decrypted data is **NEVER** written to disk during retrieval - exists in memory only and is wiped immediately after use
+ 6. **Verify Integrity**: Confirm file integrity at any time by checking the SHA-256 hash against the original record
